WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.501
-I'm freaking out.
-I'm freaking out.

00:00:02.501 --> 00:00:03.837
You're freaking out?
I'm freaking out.

00:00:03.837 --> 00:00:04.871
-I'm getting a little emotional.

00:00:04.871 --> 00:00:06.506
Look at you. Cover boy.

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:09.508
Hello! Hello! Hello!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.508 --> 00:00:11.644
-What's that pose called?

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:12.945
-You know, I love that pose.

00:00:12.945 --> 00:00:14.813
That pose is called --
What is it called?

00:00:14.813 --> 00:00:17.383
-I was talking to a friend
just now, and he said it's

00:00:17.383 --> 00:00:19.318
someone just pushed you
over the shoulder,

00:00:19.318 --> 00:00:20.753
and you're like, "Whoa!"

00:00:20.753 --> 00:00:22.122
I think that's what it is.
That's the full name.

00:00:22.122 --> 00:00:24.391
-Let me see what this is.
This one's going like...

00:00:25.592 --> 00:00:27.327
I think this one is called,

00:00:27.327 --> 00:00:29.428
"Oh, you're not going to
spoil the end for me."

00:00:29.428 --> 00:00:31.030
-Oh, yeah!
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:34.100
"I haven't seen 'Mayor of
Easttown' episode five yet.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:35.334
Don't tell me what happened."

00:00:35.334 --> 00:00:37.069
-That's the spoiler one?
-That's the spoiler one.

00:00:37.069 --> 00:00:39.872
-Congrats on "Saturday Night
Live" and everything.

00:00:39.872 --> 00:00:41.373
You're doing such a great job.

00:00:41.373 --> 00:00:43.109
This whole cast,
this whole season.

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:45.311
-Yes. Everybody.
-The writers and cast.

00:00:45.311 --> 00:00:48.415
-And crew. Everybody.
-And crew for doing this.

00:00:48.415 --> 00:00:50.683
I mean, honestly,
for pulling a show off

00:00:50.683 --> 00:00:53.720
in general is just amazing.

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:56.856
You did something on the show
a couple weeks ago

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:58.858
that got a lot of
people's attention.

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:00.893
You played the iceberg.

00:01:00.893 --> 00:01:03.763
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:03.763 --> 00:01:06.666
The iceberg
that sank the "Titanic."

00:01:06.666 --> 00:01:09.235
Where did the idea come from?
-This?

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:10.769
-Walk me through it.
-Okay.

00:01:10.769 --> 00:01:14.040
It's such a crazy journey
because the head writer

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:16.910
of "SNL," one of the head
writers, Anna Drezen,

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:18.043
an old friend of mine
from college,

00:01:18.043 --> 00:01:19.846
she texted me in February.

00:01:19.846 --> 00:01:21.814
"Hey, maybe for
the April 10th show,

00:01:21.814 --> 00:01:24.951
for the 'Titanic' anniversary,
you can play the iceberg

00:01:24.951 --> 00:01:27.253
who sank the 'Titanic.'"
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:30.022
And I was like,
"Yeah, cool. Maybe, sure."

00:01:30.022 --> 00:01:32.992
And then I kind of raised
my eyebrow at her over text.

00:01:32.992 --> 00:01:37.930
But then April rolls around
and then I text her,

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:40.766
"Hey, were you serious about
that iceberg idea?"

00:01:40.766 --> 00:01:42.801
And she was like,
"I completely forgot about it.

00:01:42.801 --> 00:01:44.170
Let's do it. Why not?"

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:46.639
And then the entire week
we did it, we just --

00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:48.408
we're losing our minds
a little bit

00:01:48.408 --> 00:01:51.177
'cause we kept looking at each
other and bursting out laughing,

00:01:51.177 --> 00:01:53.412
like, on Saturday
at like 7:00 p.m.

00:01:53.412 --> 00:01:55.981
as we were supposed to
turn in scripts.

00:01:55.981 --> 00:01:58.651
We were like,
"What are we doing?"

00:01:58.651 --> 00:01:59.785
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:59.785 --> 00:02:01.520
-"This will never make it
on to TV.

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:02.755
Will people 'get it?'

00:02:02.755 --> 00:02:04.924
Because there is just
so much going on here."

00:02:04.924 --> 00:02:07.293
-The iceberg came on "Update"
to promote --

00:02:07.293 --> 00:02:09.529
-His album.
-Yes.

00:02:09.529 --> 00:02:10.963
He has a techno --

00:02:10.963 --> 00:02:14.466
-It's a hyper-pop, EDM,
new disco fantasia.

00:02:14.466 --> 00:02:16.302
-Sorry.
-So it's a lot of genres.

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:17.436
-Yes, a lot of genres in there.

00:02:17.436 --> 00:02:18.938
And then just got upset.

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:20.839
-Got upset because he doesn't
want to be known for this thing

00:02:20.839 --> 00:02:22.041
that happened in his past

00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:24.911
and he actually feels
victimized by it.

00:02:24.911 --> 00:02:27.679
We had a line in there
that was originally,

00:02:27.679 --> 00:02:30.582
"Yes, I remember
that boat attack,"

00:02:30.582 --> 00:02:32.051
which I think is the perfect --

00:02:32.051 --> 00:02:34.621
that's what happened
when the "Titanic" sank.

00:02:34.621 --> 00:02:36.989
The iceberg was attacked by
a boat.

00:02:36.989 --> 00:02:38.825
-That's correct.
The iceberg did not move.

00:02:38.825 --> 00:02:40.292
-No.
-Yeah.

00:02:40.292 --> 00:02:42.128
It was the funniest thing.

00:02:42.128 --> 00:02:44.330
I loved it, and then it was
trending on Twitter

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:46.065
for like the next three days.
-Oh, my God.

00:02:46.065 --> 00:02:47.500
-And it was massive.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:49.936
By the way, the Mother's Day
show, your mom was fantastic.

00:02:49.936 --> 00:02:51.271
Please tell her I thought
she was so funny.

00:02:51.271 --> 00:02:52.972
Mom, you were great.
-She was great.

00:02:52.972 --> 00:02:55.108
-The Purell.
-Purell.

00:02:55.108 --> 00:02:57.043
She could handle a prop bit.

00:02:57.043 --> 00:02:59.178
-Was she nervous?
-She was very nervous.

00:02:59.178 --> 00:03:00.379
She wouldn't tell me
she was nervous,

00:03:00.379 --> 00:03:02.182
but everyone complimented her
in the studio.

00:03:02.182 --> 00:03:04.116
Like, "You handled the props
great."

00:03:04.116 --> 00:03:06.385
She's like the Carrot Top
and Gallagher of moms.

00:03:06.385 --> 00:03:08.487
[ Laughter ]
-She really is.

00:03:08.487 --> 00:03:09.989
-She is.

00:03:09.989 --> 00:03:11.824
-Oh, my goodness.
That's so funny.

00:03:11.824 --> 00:03:14.227
I remember my mom was
on the Mother's Day thing.

00:03:14.227 --> 00:03:15.895
And she was so nervous.

00:03:15.895 --> 00:03:18.064
She was freaking out,
and I remember at the beginning,

00:03:18.064 --> 00:03:19.832
we did a monologue
with all the moms.

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:22.601
Everyone's there, you know, with
their moms or dads, you know.

00:03:22.601 --> 00:03:23.736
And we're all standing around.

00:03:23.736 --> 00:03:26.039
And I got something in my eye.
-[ Gasps ]

00:03:26.039 --> 00:03:28.274
-If you ever want to see
a disaster, get something

00:03:28.274 --> 00:03:30.510
in your eye when there's 30 moms
on stage.

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:31.643
[ Laughter ]
Because I go like --

00:03:31.643 --> 00:03:33.245
Someone's going,
"Hold your lid out

00:03:33.245 --> 00:03:34.414
and roll your eye back."

00:03:34.414 --> 00:03:36.349
"Blow in it!"
"No, put water in it!"

00:03:36.349 --> 00:03:37.683
"No, blowing will be fine."
Grabbing my head.

00:03:37.683 --> 00:03:39.051
I was like,
"Okay, guys, hold on."

00:03:39.051 --> 00:03:41.321
-That's beautiful to be
screamed at by that many moms.

00:03:41.321 --> 00:03:43.656
-It was a fantastic Mother's Day
moment for me.

00:03:43.656 --> 00:03:44.790
-Yeah.

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:46.391
-I follow you on Instagram,
by the way.

00:03:46.391 --> 00:03:49.128
I follow @fayedunaway.

00:03:49.128 --> 00:03:51.197
-@Fayedunaway is the handle,
yes.

00:03:51.197 --> 00:03:53.032
-I just think
that's interesting.

00:03:53.032 --> 00:03:55.802
-Yeah. It's interesting.

00:03:55.802 --> 00:04:00.973
All I want is for Faye Dunaway,
the real Oscar-winning actress,

00:04:00.973 --> 00:04:04.043
to, like, sue me or something.

00:04:04.043 --> 00:04:05.277
[ Laughter ]

00:04:05.277 --> 00:04:07.246
-Would you go to court?
-I would go to court.

00:04:07.246 --> 00:04:10.717
I would get locked into, like,
the longest battle with her.

00:04:10.717 --> 00:04:12.918
No, all I want is just --
-Talk to her.

00:04:12.918 --> 00:04:15.287
A cease and desist or -- Yeah.

00:04:15.287 --> 00:04:16.822
-She's watching. Faye.

00:04:16.822 --> 00:04:18.791
-Faye? Faye Dunaway.
-Legendary.

00:04:18.791 --> 00:04:20.859
-Legendary actress Faye Dunaway.
-Amazing, gorgeous.

00:04:20.859 --> 00:04:23.996
-All I want is for you
to reach out to me

00:04:23.996 --> 00:04:28.534
and call me
"that sniveling homosexual."

00:04:28.534 --> 00:04:31.203
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.203 --> 00:04:32.672
-That's not what you want.

00:04:32.672 --> 00:04:34.740
-Yes, it is what I want!
It is what I want!

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:38.144
Because she's fantastic

00:04:38.144 --> 00:04:39.946
and I just want her
to insult me and say,

00:04:39.946 --> 00:04:41.147
"You give that handle to me.

00:04:41.147 --> 00:04:43.249
I want to be on Instagram
with everybody else."

00:04:43.249 --> 00:04:45.117
-I don't think she would care
about Instagram,

00:04:45.117 --> 00:04:48.220
but I think that she cares about
you and that you love her,

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:50.589
and I think that she would say,
"Hey, you know what?

00:04:50.589 --> 00:04:51.824
You've got my blessing."

00:04:51.824 --> 00:04:53.259
-Wow! I hope that happens.

00:04:53.259 --> 00:04:55.428
-"And I love you and congrats on
your success, Bowen Yang."

00:04:55.428 --> 00:04:57.163
-Jimmy, thanks so much
for having me.

00:04:57.163 --> 00:04:59.599
-Dude, you're the greatest, bud.
I'm so happy for you, pal.

00:04:59.599 --> 00:05:01.100
Bowen Yang.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:04.537
The season finale of "Saturday
Night Live" airs this Saturday.

